WEBVTT

00:00:00.860 --> 00:00:03.516
Students join with individual codes.

00:00:03.556 --> 00:00:08.962
Today’s question: should nuclear power be
part of a low-carbon electricity system?

00:00:10.063 --> 00:00:13.376
Alex: Could nuclear power help
provide reliable electricity?

00:00:14.478 --> 00:00:17.095
Sam: How should we weigh
cost and construction time?

00:00:18.196 --> 00:00:21.557
Priya: What about waste,
safety and public acceptance?

00:00:22.658 --> 00:00:24.903
Later, positions have been repeated.

00:00:25.098 --> 00:00:29.830
This activity’s moderation profile
calls for comparing the reasoning.

00:00:30.931 --> 00:00:32.933
Moderator: What evidence supports each view?

00:00:33.069 --> 00:00:36.290
Moderator: Which shared criteria
could help you compare the options?

00:00:37.391 --> 00:00:40.334
Alex: Let’s check sources
for our reliability claims.

00:00:41.435 --> 00:00:44.656
Sam: Could we compare options
over the same time period?

00:00:45.757 --> 00:00:48.606
Priya: Let’s include safety
and public acceptance.

00:00:49.708 --> 00:00:52.650
Educators determine the moderator’s role.

00:00:52.787 --> 00:00:58.460
Students examine evidence, connect
perspectives and develop their own conclusions.
